From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: take the coprocessor DARTs through a
 firmware suspend

A firmware-driven sleep resets every DART. After the first real wake on
T8140 every RTKit coprocessor but the DCP timed out: the PMP and SIO
restart their firmware in their early resume, and their first DMA went
through a DART that had not been put back yet.

- For a firmware-driven sleep, suspend and resume in the noirq phase,
  which every device finishes before any early resume, and after a real
  sleep write the saved state back even for a DART runtime PM had
  suspended, which pm_runtime_force_resume() leaves alone. Every other
  sleep keeps the normal phase, on every SoC: the PCIe-C tunnel DARTs
  need it, as their host stops the tunnel ports in its suspend_noirq
  and sets the port clock up again in its resume_noirq. On Apple SoCs
  only the T8140 sleep driver, later in this series, sets
  pm_suspend_via_firmware(), from .begin, and it holds until the next
  suspend, so both halves take the same phase.
- Replay the loader's address filter. The PMP's first write after the
  wake lands in a range the loader programs into its DART's DAPF (the
  ADT's dapf-instance-0), which a real sleep clears. Take the ranges
  from apple,dapf-ranges and an optional apple,dapf-r20, and write them
  back wherever the translations are restored, unless the filter still
  holds them or is locked.
- Write the loader's tunables back where a power-off lost them, from
  apple,resume-tunable, only the words that differ. The ISP's DARTs need
  both, as its firmware starts again after the wake.
- A consumer-driven save and restore for a DART whose firmware gates
  itself before the DARTs suspend (the SEP's): apple,sleep-prepare,
  apple,sleep-restore and apple,sleep-restore-late list the writes
  around it, and the consumer calls apple_dart_sleep_prepare() and
  apple_dart_sleep_restore() in its own order. The DART's own callbacks
  then leave it alone. Its config words go back as the DART had them
  before the sleep, since Linux's setup of those words differs from
  macOS's.
- GAPF. On T8140 the fabric rejects a write to a display coprocessor's
  CPU power state while bit 4 of its DART's GAPF slice is set. A display
  stop that flushes the DART waits for the flush, then clears the bit;
  it's set again when the streams come back on.
  apple_dart_display_streams() does macOS's stream writes for a display
  power cycle. A deep sleep resets the GAPF bank too, so the slice's
  value is saved at probe and protected with that, and
  apple_dart_gapf_ready() releases a slice the wake left protected
  before the coprocessor's CPU domain comes up.
- While a display DART's streams are off for a power-down its registers
  may be unpowered: take each stream's table level from a snapshot made
  as they went off, and defer TLB invalidations until the streams are
  back on. apple_dart_power_dark() does the same for a display DART
  whose domain goes off at runtime while others still map into it: the
  display subsystem maps every framebuffer into DCPEXT's DART, and a map
  during DCPEXT's power cycle read a TCR in the unpowered DART.
- A DART that runs on its PCIe port's clock, as the T8140 radio port's
  does, gates itself in its noirq resume after a real sleep, until its
  host has the port back and calls apple_dart_host_resume(). The first
  real sleep with the radio host bound took an SError there.
- apple_dart_state_save() and apple_dart_state_restore() keep a DART's
  state across its consumer's own power cycle, outside a system sleep.
  They return -ENODEV for a device apple-dart isn't bound to.

DARTs with none of these properties, and other sleeps, behave as before.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>

[j604 backport: kept our retained-display/dcpext/MTP board lists beside the new sleep-list helpers; resume keeps our host_off gate beside sleep_saved and host_resumes; Aurora-only cold_ane dropped; tools/asahi fixtures kept as ours; no J604 DART carries apple,dapf-ranges/apple,resume-tunable yet (T3 DT data, from the J604 ADT)]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5

